license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: 2026-05-21
abstract: >
  SbD-ToE MCP is an installable Model Context Protocol (MCP) server providing
  citation-backed, ontology-grounded retrieval over a Security-by-Design
  practitioner manual. The 15-chapter manual corpus is normalized against
  thirty-one external sources (frameworks, standards, regulations) and bound
  to AppSec Core v1, a typed ontology of 259 entities across ten domain slices.
  All knowledge artefacts are derived from frozen, SHA-256-pinned releases of
  the upstream AppSec Core research programme (papers P1, P6, P7, P8). The
  server runs offline, requires no API keys, and integrates with Claude,
  GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Windsurf, Zed, and other MCP-compatible clients.

  Note on licensing: the code in this repository is released under Apache-2.0;
  the bundled data artefacts derived from the SbD-ToE practitioner manual are
  released under CC-BY-SA-4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA and LICENSE-NOTE.md).
